Run 1 (a person says Enter, H is the `roc` on PATH, N missing): `init` makes an app. The prompt names N alone (R-NI12, default yes). The header has the newest `roc-lang/basic-cli` that min-release-age allows (0.25.0, not the 1-day-old 0.26.0), `roc: <N>` and the hello world. A CI file is written, with the version of `tln`. The project file is recorded in `projects.json` (R-PD9). No `.roc-version` and no `talon.toml` (R-IN4, R-IN5, R-SO16). The download does not set the default compiler (R-SO15: `init` is no user act for the default), so the tree has no `config.toml`.
Run 2 (CI, `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=no`, `--ci none`): the newest nightly starts with no prompt and no refusal (R-DL4, R-NI12: the command names it). No `.github` dir (R-IN6).
Run 3 (`init app --yes`, a person): `--yes` accepts the prompt (R-NI12, R-DL5). No `ask` call.
Run 4 (CI, `min-release-age = "0d"` in `config.toml`): the start release is 0.26.0 and N is n14 (R-C7, R-UP6). The download starts in CI.
Run 5 (`--platform acme/pfx`, all compilers installed): another platform. The header has pfx, and the body is the stub app of R-IN8 (slice 055: `main! = || crash "write the app"`, from the `requires` clause of the platform; before slice 055 it was the smallest `main!`). pfx 0.2.0 fails the unit check on n12, so the pin is n11 and the note names n12 (R-IN2: the newest platform release and the newest nightly that pass). The release 0.2.0 is kept, the compiler is the last slot of the search.
Run 6 (`init package`): a package header with the pin, 2 probes (a package has no build, R-LD7). The CI file is the same.
Run 7 (`main.roc` is in the directory already): exit 2. No file changes, no `projects.json` entry, no index call (R-IN7). The file is kept byte for byte.
Run 8 (a directory below one that has `main.roc` and a `talon.toml` with `[workspace]`): `init` writes `i8/sub/main.roc`. It does not search up for a project, and the files above do not stop it (R-PD15).
Run 9 (`--json`): the envelope has `command` `init`. `data.written` has `main.roc` and the CI file (a proposal, TW24).
Run 10 (`init lib`): exit 2, the template name is wrong (R-IN1, R-EC2). No call except `args`.
Run 11 (a person says n, N missing): exit 13, nothing downloaded. `main.roc` was written before the flow, so the run removes it (it made it): the directory has no file after the run and `init` can run again (answer Q1 of the review). The record in `projects.json` stays (GC drops an entry with no file, R-PD13).
Run 12 (`.github/workflows/ci.yml` exists): `main.roc` is written, the CI file is not overwritten (R-IN7), the line `note: .github/workflows/ci.yml exists, not written` is printed, exit 0 (answer Q2).
Run 13 (CI, `--allow-downloads`, `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` names n10, which is not installed): the baseline compiler is a required download, and `--allow-downloads` answers it (R-IN3, R-DL5, answer Q3). The line `downloading 2 compilers`: n10 and N.
Run 14 (gap, `--platform acme/young`, its only release is 1 day old): min-release-age (2 days) hides it, so `Init.start` finds none. Exit 2, `no release of acme/young is old enough for min-release-age`. `main.roc` is not written (the failure comes before the first write).
